Found five significant authorization issues at commit ef5cf09:
[P1] assignRole validates the supplied organization, but never verifies the target user belongs to it. An admin can modify a cross-tenant account and issue mismatched custom claims.
[P1] setPermissionOverrides has the same missing target-organization check.
[P1] Any authenticated organization member—including students—can create arbitrary payment records.
[P1] Many update rules validate only the existing organizationId, allowing staff to move documents into another tenant by changing that field.
[P1] New owners receive tenantId: "default", while tenant rules treat matching tenant IDs as authorization. Owners can therefore access or update other organizations’ "default" tenant records.
Additional review found seven more issues:
[P1] Students can create submissions containing forged grades/statuses.
[P1] Students can edit answers after submission.
[P1] Parents can approve their own pending student link.
[P1] Any scoped teacher can disable any student in the organization.
[P1] The password callable does not enforce recent authentication.
[P2] Organization archival exceeds Firestore’s 500-write batch limit.
[P2] Confirmed organization deletion can orphan exam-dependent records.
